simulator | unwanted_factor | S2 | value | normal sample scores; normal loadings with variance 3 x 0.09, added to the complete precursor matrix before missing values are drawn | sim/s2_limpa.R header
simulator | unwanted_factor | S3 | value | sample scores with mean 0 and variance 1; normal loadings on the log2 mean; variance of the loadings 3 x the median residual variance of log2 counts | sim/s3_trx.R header
simulator | unwanted_factor | S4 | value | two components, drift exp(-2u) along injection order and a sample-wise factor, with normal loadings; their variance together 3 x the median residual variance (0.75), split equally | sim/s4_lipid_metab.R header
simulator | factor_group_correlation | S1 | value | exact by construction | sim/s1_classic.R header
simulator | factor_group_correlation | S2 | value | in expectation; the realised value varies from data set to data set | sim/s2_limpa.R header
simulator | factor_group_correlation | S3 | value | exact by construction | sim/s3_trx.R header
simulator | factor_group_correlation | S4 | value | sample-wise factor exact; drift: the injection order nearest the target among 2,000 random orders | sim/s4_lipid_metab.R header
simulator | missing_values | S1 | value | intensity dependent, P(missing) = plogis(limit - value), the limit solved per data set for the scenario's share; a protein is kept when at least half of each group's samples are observed | sim/s1_classic.R header
simulator | missing_values | S2 | value | detection probability curve of the function, P(missing) = plogis(intercept + 0.7 y, lower.tail = FALSE), drawn after the effects and the factor are added | sim/s2_limpa.R header
simulator | missing_values | S3 | value | none (counts); genes pass edgeR::filterByExpr | sim/s3_trx.R header
simulator | missing_values | S4 | value | one detection limit per assay at the scenario's share of all candidate values; a feature is kept when observed at least once in every group, so the share among kept features is lower | sim/s4_lipid_metab.R header
simulator | pooled_qc | S4 | value | a pooled QC injection first, after every 5 study injections and after the last | sim/s4_lipid_metab.R header
simulator | test | S1 | value | limma through the package's kernel: ~ 0 + group, treat with a cutoff of 0, eBayes with trend and robust; duplicateCorrelation on the unit where technical replicates are declared | sim/s1_classic.R header
simulator | test | S2 | value | DPC quantification (engine fastlimpadpc), then limpa::dpcDE with ~ 0 + group, the technical-replicate block where declared, eBayes with trend and robust | sim/s2_limpa.R header
simulator | test | S3 | value | edgeR quasi-likelihood: TMM, estimateDisp(robust), glmQLFit(robust), glmQLFTest | sim/s3_trx.R header
simulator | test | S4 | value | limma per assay and contrast: lmFit, contrasts.fit, eBayes with trend and robust; no replicate block | sim/s4_lipid_metab.R header
simulator | call | S1 | value | q below 0.05 (qvalue::qvalue; Benjamini-Hochberg where it fails) | sim/s1_classic.R header
simulator | call | S2 | value | q below 0.05 (qvalue::qvalue; Benjamini-Hochberg where it cannot run) | sim/s2_limpa.R header
simulator | call | S3 | value | Benjamini-Hochberg FDR below 0.05 | sim/s3_trx.R header
simulator | call | S4 | value | q below 0.05 per assay and contrast (qvalue::qvalue; Benjamini-Hochberg where it fails) | sim/s4_lipid_metab.R header
simulator | scoring_unit | S1 | value | one false discovery proportion per data set, over the proteins of the scored contrast | sim/s1_classic.R header
simulator | scoring_unit | S2 | value | one false discovery proportion per data set, over the quantified proteins | sim/s2_limpa.R header
