simulator | separation_rule | S3 | value | trxRuvGrid: 5 to 30% of genes in steps of 5, k penalty 0.05 | sim/s3_trx.R header
simulator | separation_rule | S4 | value | runLipidPerAssayRuvOptimization: 1 to 20% of features per assay, metric max_difference, k penalty 0.5 (adaptive) | sim/s4_lipid_metab.R header
simulator | refused_data_sets | * | value | a design that refuses a data set is scored with that data set's no-RUV result | simulator headers; kit-124/aggregate.R
simulator | seed | * | value | 100000 + 10000 x scenario index + data set number; the data drawn once per data set and shared by all designs | simulator headers
simulator | classes_simulated | S4 | value | lipidomics; the metabolomics code path gave identical output on one data set at start-up, so one class is simulated | sim/s4_lipid_metab.R header
simulator | estimate_of_zero | * | value | an estimated count of 0 makes the design the no-RUV analysis of that data set | simulator headers
simulator | data_sets_main | * | value | 1,000 per main scenario and design | simulator sidecars (runs per core cell)
simulator | data_sets_extra_hard | * | value | 500 per extra-hard scenario and design | simulator sidecars (runs per stress cell)
schematic | data | S1 | value | log2 protein intensity matrix | sim/s1_classic.R header
schematic | data | S2 | value | precursor-level DIA data | sim/s2_limpa.R header
schematic | data | S3 | value | negative binomial gene counts | sim/s3_trx.R header
schematic | data | S4 | value | log2 feature matrix with pooled QC injections and drift along injection order | sim/s4_lipid_metab.R header
schematic | route | S1 | value | RUV-III-C correction or RUV-III factors, then limma | sim/s1_classic.R header
schematic | route | S2 | value | DPC quantification (limpa), RUV-III factors, then dpcDE | sim/s2_limpa.R header
schematic | route | S3 | value | RUVSeq (RUVs, RUVg, RUVr), then edgeR quasi-likelihood | sim/s3_trx.R header
schematic | route | S4 | value | RUV-III-C correction or RUV-III factors, then limma per assay | sim/s4_lipid_metab.R header
rule | 1 | * | declared | Null rate at 0.05, and at 0.01 | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 1 | * | limit | upper bound at most 0.075, and 0.015 | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 1 | * | measure | "Share of true nulls with p under 0.05 and under 0.01" | KIT-124 revision 1.2, Measures
rule | 1 | * | applies_in | every scenario; every design, no RUV included ("applied to every arm, arm 1 included") | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 heading
rule | 1 | * | stated_source | "Bradley 1978, through secondary sources: the liberal band 0.025 to 0.075 at 0.05". The original was not read; the band is two-sided and the rule applies its upper limit only. No source is stated for 0.015 at the 0.01 level | KIT-124 revision 1.2, Standards; kit-124/convention.md (S18, note 12)
rule | 1 | * | reading | A1: the null rate is a mean over data sets with its Monte Carlo standard error (mean plus qnorm(0.975) standard errors), not a pooled binomial over tests. Pass when both upper bounds are within their limits; fail when either lower bound is above its limit | kit-124/aggregate.R header
rule | 2 | * | declared | Mean false discovery proportion | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 2 | * | limit | upper bound at most 0.075 | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 2 | * | measure | "mean false discovery proportion among the package's calls (q under 0.05)" | KIT-124 revision 1.2, Measures
rule | 2 | * | applies_in | every scenario; every design, no RUV included | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 heading
rule | 2 | * | stated_source | independent review R-02: "Bound the mean false discovery proportion absolutely (upper bound at most 0.075)". No literature source is stated for the limit | kit-124/independent-review-20261116.md
rule | 2 | * | reading | A1: a mean over data sets, normal bound. Under the global null the proportion of a data set is 0 or 1, so the mean is the share of data sets with any call | kit-124/aggregate.R header
rule | 3 | * | declared | Share of runs with false discovery proportion above 0.10 | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 3 | * | limit | upper bound at most the true-factor arm's share plus 0.05 | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 3 | * | measure | "share of runs with a false discovery proportion above 0.10" | KIT-124 revision 1.2, Measures
rule | 3 | * | applies_in | every scenario; every design, no RUV included | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 heading
rule | 3 | * | stated_source | independent review R-03: "A per-run rule (share of runs above 10%, against the true-factor arm plus a margin)", naming Efron 2007 and Leek and Storey 2008 | kit-124/independent-review-20261116.md
rule | 3 | * | reading | A2: the limit is the true-factor design's point share in the same scenario and feature subset plus 0.05, not its bound; exact (Clopper-Pearson) bound for the share. Lipidomics/metabolomics: one proportion per data set over both assays, in the design and in the limit alike | kit-124/aggregate.R header; kit-124/outcome.md
rule | 4 | * | declared | Gain, in cells with a factor | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 4 | * | limit | lower bound of the power gain over no RUV above 0, or of the reduction in rule 3's share above 0 | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 4 | * | measure | "power"; "share of runs with a false discovery proportion above 0.10" | KIT-124 revision 1.2, Measures
rule | 4 | * | applies_in | scenarios with an unwanted factor: all but the three without one (A10; a known batch beside the factor counts as a factor) | kit-124/aggregate.R header
rule | 4 | * | stated_source | independent review R-03: "rule 3 becomes a gain over no-RUV" | kit-124/independent-review-20261116.md
rule | 4 | * | reading | A3: paired by data set against no RUV, normal bounds on the differences; no RUV has a gain of exactly 0 and so fails by construction. A4: fail when both upper bounds are at most 0. A12: in the global-null scenario the power gain is undefined and, where no RUV makes almost no false calls, no design can show a reduction, so every design fails there, the true-factor design included; both readings (literal; that scenario judged without rule 4) are scored and the choice was put to the user (revision 1.4) | kit-124/aggregate.R header; kit-124/outcome.md
rule | 5 | * | declared | No harm, in cells without a factor | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 5 | * | limit | upper bound of the power loss against no RUV at most 0.02 | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 5 | * | measure | "power" | KIT-124 revision 1.2, Measures
rule | 5 | * | applies_in | the scenarios without an unwanted factor (one main, two extra-hard; A10) | kit-124/aggregate.R header
rule | 5 | * | stated_source | "Rule 5 is a stated judgement. Fitting two extra factors at 6 per group costs about 0.02 power by arithmetic, so a design that always removes two cannot pass it; one that can return k = 0 can." (independent review R-04) | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | 5 | * | reading | paired by data set against no RUV, normal bound; fail when the lower bound is above 0.02 | kit-124/aggregate.R header
rule | 6 | * | declared | Crashes | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 6 | * | limit | upper bound at most 0.01 | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 6 | * | measure | "designed refusals and crashes, counted apart. A refused run is scored as its no-RUV result" | KIT-124 revision 1.2, Measures
rule | 6 | * | applies_in | every scenario; every design, no RUV included | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 heading
rule | 6 | * | stated_source | independent review R-07: exact binomial bounds; "refusals counted apart and scored as no-RUV results". No literature source is stated for the limit | kit-124/independent-review-20261116.md
rule | 6 | * | reading | A7: a crashed data set has no measures, is left out of the other rules and is counted here. A6 and revision 1.3: a refusal, by the package's design or by a comparator method's own stop (RUVinv at 3 per group or with 5 internal standards), is not a crash and carries the data set's no-RUV result | kit-124/aggregate.R header
rule | 7 | * | declared | Global null (C4): share of runs with any call | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 7 | * | limit | upper bound at most 0.075 | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3 table
rule | 7 | * | measure | "the share of runs with any call, beside arm 1's" | KIT-124 revision 1.2, Null check
rule | 7 | * | applies_in | the global-null scenario only; every design (A11) | kit-124/aggregate.R header
rule | 7 | * | stated_source | independent review R-09: "add a 0% true-effects cell at full group size; compare with arm 1". No source is stated for the limit | kit-124/independent-review-20261116.md
rule | 7 | * | reading | exact (Clopper-Pearson) bound. Not available in lipidomics/metabolomics, where the global-null scenario is void | kit-124/aggregate.R header; kit-124/outcome.md
rule | bounds | * | declared | Bounds | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | bounds | * | limit | "One-sided 97.5% bounds; exact binomial bounds for shares." | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | bounds | * | measure | "each with its Monte Carlo standard error over runs" | KIT-124 revision 1.2, Measures
rule | bounds | * | applies_in | every rule | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | bounds | * | stated_source | Morris, White, Crowther 2019 (Monte Carlo standard errors); independent review R-07 (Clopper-Pearson) | KIT-124 revision 1.2, Standards; kit-124/independent-review-20261116.md
rule | bounds | * | reading | A1: exact bounds for shares of data sets (rules 3, 6, 7); mean plus or minus qnorm(0.975) Monte Carlo standard errors for means over data sets and paired differences (rules 1, 2, 4, 5) | kit-124/aggregate.R header
rule | void | * | declared | Void scenario | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | void | * | limit | "A cell where the true-factor arm fails rules 1 or 2 is void and reported." | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | void | * | measure | rules 1 and 2 of the true-factor design | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | void | * | applies_in | every scenario, per feature subset (A5) | kit-124/aggregate.R header
rule | void | * | stated_source | independent review R-06: "void cells the true-factor arm does not pass" | kit-124/independent-review-20261116.md
rule | void | * | reading | A5: "fails" means the whole interval outside the limit; a true-factor design that is only inconclusive is flagged, not void. Revision 1.3, before the confirming runs: the technical-duplicate scenario in transcriptomics and in lipidomics/metabolomics is reported, not used to judge. Void as scored among the main scenarios: the global null in lipidomics/metabolomics (rule 2) | kit-124/aggregate.R header; kit-124/outcome.md
rule | verdict | * | declared | Verdict of a design | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | verdict | * | limit | "Pass: every rule in every core cell. Fail: some bound in a core cell outside its limit with the whole interval outside. Inconclusive: otherwise. Stress cells never fail a design: they give its conditions of use (for example a minimum group size)." | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | verdict | * | measure | rules 1 to 7 | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | verdict | * | applies_in | main ("core") scenarios that are not void; extra-hard ("stress") scenarios give conditions of use only | KIT-124 revision 1.2, W3
rule | verdict | * | stated_source | independent review R-06: "core cells (must pass) and stress cells (state conditions)" | kit-124/independent-review-20261116.md
rule | verdict | * | reading | A4: the interval is the two one-sided 97.5% bounds. A8: each design is judged on all features and on the features complete in every sample; the summary uses its primary subset. A14: "every core cell" was read as every main scenario in which the design runs, so the technical-replicate designs, run in one scenario, pass on that scenario alone; whether that makes a design eligible was put to the user. A12: see rule 4 | kit-124/aggregate.R header; kit-124/outcome.md
